 ### Start
 
-1. Run `login` in the background. It signs in with the saved session, the remembered SSO session or the saved password, and only when all fail opens a local sign-in page and prints its URL for the user. Never ask for or handle the password yourself.
+1. In Hermes, the delegated worker prepares the session with `mcp__personal__campus_login_start` before online commands. It reuses valid cookies and reads the age-managed credentials itself. If it returns `verification_required`, report the masked phone to the coordinating agent, then use `campus_login_submit` for the user's reply on the same MCP connection. Continue after `authenticated`. Do not open a WebUI or read credentials. A later authentication error means renewing through these tools and retrying the requested command.
 2. Find the course with `courses` (enrolled courses, latest term first) or `search` (the whole platform); ask only when several courses match.
 3. Run `add <course>` for a new course. For an existing course folder, read `课程总结.md` and run `status` instead.
 
